| the same, with `spring.profiles.active: zzz` set in `etc/application.yml` instead | `FAIL …/application-aaa.yml, …` | `FAIL …/application-aaa.yml or …/application-zzz.yml, line 2, column 1: …` |

alpha.112 was then installed on the same database. `start` and `verify --tenant e2e --turn` pass, with `PASS config` for both files inside `--check --online`.

The new name rule is still exact against the configuration reference: 9 secrets of 182, none missed and none extra.

The sweep had 15 mutants, run as uid 1000: 12 killed on the first pass. Of the three survivors:
- Stripping separators before the suffix test changes nothing, since a lowercased element ends in `key` either way, so that code was removed.
