## What Problem This Solves

Fixes: updating direct dependencies leaves older transitive copies that still match public advisories for Joi, RE2JS, Undici and Zod 4.

## User Impact

IMAP's mailauth and the Copilot SDK resolve patched dependencies; RE2JS in development tooling is patched too. Existing parent packages, major APIs and Zod 3 compatibility remain in place. No configuration or migration is required. This is dependency remediation, not a claim of a demonstrated deployed exploit or a vulnerability-free installation.

## Why This Change Was Made

Same-major version-scoped overrides address the actual remaining consumers without upgrading mailauth to a version that downgrades other dependencies. Reuse the root's qualified Undici 8.12.3 and Zod 4.6.7; move Joi 18.2.9 to 18.3.1 and RE2JS 2.8.6 to 2.8.7. No package major changes, new patches, release-age exclusions or global age-policy changes.

Public advisories and affected parent paths are recorded in the issue. All selected versions satisfy the existing seven-day release-age policy. Retirement: remove each override after every parent resolves a patched version without it.

